  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Let the Good Times Roll** (1 review): Listener asks who is singing on this song, starting a little after the two-minute mark [4]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **West L.A. Fadeaway**: back after 56 archived shows (697 days) [5]\n- **Grateful Dead News Broadcast**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2024-06-08.2024-06-08.unknown-mics.montanari.carpeneter.flac.2448** (recommended): audience recording; 21 songs; 170 min [1]. Said about its sound: The patched sections were equalized and level-adjusted to match the rest of the recording for consistency [1]\n- **deadco2024-06-08**: source not stated; 20 songs; 176 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2024-06-08.2024-06-08.unknown-mics.montanari.carpeneter.flac.2448**: taped by Neil Montanari; transferred by Ted Carpenter; source: Aud - unknown mics -> SD premix 6 -> Wav 24bit 48kh [1]. Also: Source was completed by patching in Deal, Knockin' on Heaven's Door, the news broadcast and Not Fade Away from another upload [1]\n- **deadco2024-06-08**: taped by Cam Keough; transferred by Cam Keough; source: Church Audio CA-14 (Cards) -> Naiant Tinyhead-> Rode AI Micro-> Pixel 5 (24/48) [2]. Also: Chain: Church Audio CA-14 cardioid mics, Naiant Tinyhead, Rode AI Micro, Pixel 5 at 24-bit/48k; then Adobe Audition, CD Wave, THL [2]",
